sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ga02-09> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Nature orders generation in a regular gradation: the hottest and most perfect animals bear live young internally, then come those viviparous after internal eggs, then those laying perfect eggs, then those laying imperfect eggs, and coldest of all those producing a scolex.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Nature orders generation in a graded series by heat and perfection";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, On the Generation of Animals (De Generatione Animalium), Book II; translated by Arthur Platt, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. V (1912). Scope: All animals, from mammals to insects"
}
